 ## Overview
-Premoze et al. path integration is an approximation for simulating light transport in participating media that utilizes the WKB (Wentzel-Kramers-Brillouin) approximation to compute multiply-scattered light [S1]. It is distinguished from the diffusion approximation by its validity in sparse and inhomogeneous media, though it assumes strongly forward-peaked phase functions and ignores backscattering [S1]. It builds on [WKB-based Multiple Scattering Approximation](1490-wkb-based-multiple-scattering-approximation.md).
